 FCP is a UDP tunnel with adaptive forward error correction and a stream
 layer on top. This package installs the two CLI ends:
 .
  * fcp-server -- listens on one UDP port and dials the targets a
    client asks for (SOCKS5 / HTTP CONNECT semantics);
  * fcp-client -- opens a local SOCKS5 / HTTP CONNECT entry
    (default 127.0.0.1:1080) and carries its traffic over FCP.
 .
 The package ships a systemd unit for the server side; start-up arguments
 live in /etc/fcp/fcp.env (a dpkg conffile, so upgrades keep your
 edits). The service is not started on install: you must supply a
 pre-shared key first (see /usr/share/doc/fcp/部署运维指南.md).
 .
 FCP v7 does not interoperate with v6: both ends must run the same major
 wire version.
